    "interpretation": "Open-market trades filed from 2023, when the checkbox first existed, so the classifier never saw this label. Routine-labelled trades are filed under a pre-scheduled 10b5-1 plan 54.7% of the time against 39.0% for opportunistic ones (odds ratio 1.89); restricted to open-market purchases, the subset the signal actually trades, the rates are 13.3% and 3.5%. The gap survives collapsing to one observation per insider-year, so it is not an artifact of a few prolific sellers. Agreement is directional rather than exact: precision and recall near 0.6 mean the behavioral proxy and the checkbox disagree on a large minority of trades, which is the measurement error the pre-2023 sample carries silently."
